# Infisical Universal Auth bootstrap credentials.
#
# These are the only variables you provide yourself. varlock uses them to
# authenticate to the Infisical project (see @initInfisical in .env.schema)
# and resolve every other variable through the infisical() resolver.
# Everything else lives in Infisical and is fetched at dev time, or synced
# into Vercel at build time, so nothing else belongs in this file.
#
# Provide them either by exporting from your shell (the project reads them
# from ~/.zshenv) or by copying this file to a local, gitignored .env.
# Then start the dev server with `bun dev` (which runs `varlock run -- nuxt dev`).
#
# Create the machine identity in Infisical:
#   Access Control > Machine Identities > Create Identity > Universal Auth
# Grant it read-only access to this project, then copy its Client ID and
# Client Secret below.
# https://infisical.com/docs/documentation/platform/identities/universal-auth

INFISICAL_CLIENT_ID=""
INFISICAL_CLIENT_SECRET=""
